# Gurudevi Web — The Full Mastery Plan

## Part 1: The One Real Bug  

**Single cause of white screen:** `expo-camera` is imported *unconditionally at the top* of [packages/scanner-kit/src/ScannerModal.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Naween/projects/polymath-platform/packages/scanner-kit/src/ScannerModal.tsx). This throws before React mounts.

**Fix:** `ScannerModal.web.tsx` — Pattern A (platform file pair, no shim, no metro change).

> Everything else (reanimated, haptics, mmkv, skia, flash-list, gesture-handler) is already handled.

---

## Part 2: Web-Excellence Additions  
*Where web beats mobile — and we should lean in.*

### 2a — PWA: Make it Installable

**What:** Teachers on Chromebook/desktop can "install" the app without an app store.  
**How:** Extend `app.json → web` section.

#### [MODIFY] [app.json](file:///c:/Users/Naween/projects/polymath-platform/apps/gurudevi-mobile/app.json)
```json
"web": {
  "favicon": "./assets/favicon.png",
  "bundler": "metro",
  "baseUrl": "/",
  "name": "Gurudevi",
  "shortName": "Gurudevi",
  "lang": "en",
  "display": "standalone",
  "themeColor": "#D4843A",
  "backgroundColor": "#F5EDD6",
  "description": "A sacred space for teachers — wellbeing, classroom, and community."
}
```

> This generates a `manifest.json` that makes the app installable as a PWA. Zero dependencies.

---

### 2b — Hover States (Desktop UX)

**What:** `Pressable` on mobile has no concept of hover. On web, teachers using a mouse get no feedback. We can add this to any `Pressable`-based button in `@repo/ui` components.  
**How:** `Pressable` exposes `onHoverIn`/`onHoverOut` on web (via react-native-web). Wire them with a local state flag → adjust opacity or shadow.

This is a **Pattern C** (inline `Platform.select`) change to `SanctuaryCard`, `LotusPetalFAB`, and key action buttons.

#### [MODIFY] [packages/ui/src/components/SanctuaryCard.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Naween/projects/polymath-platform/packages/ui/src/components/SanctuaryCard.tsx)

```tsx
// Add web hover state via Pressable
const [hovered, setHovered] = useState(false);

<Pressable
  onHoverIn={() => Platform.OS === 'web' && setHovered(true)}
  onHoverOut={() => Platform.OS === 'web' && setHovered(false)}
  style={[styles.card, hovered && styles.cardHovered]}
/>

// cardHovered: { opacity: 0.92, transform: [{ scale: 1.01 }] }
```

---

### 2c — Keyboard Navigation (Desktop Power)

**What:** No RN app expects keyboard navigation. On web, teachers can tab through dashboard cards, press Enter on actions.  
**How:** Wrap key interactive areas with `onKeyDown` handlers (Pattern C).

Priority targets (highest ROI):
- **Auth screen** — Enter key on password field to submit login
- **AI Assistant** — Enter to send message  
- **QR Code input** (in ScannerModal.web.tsx) — Enter to submit pasted code

These go directly into the [.web.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Naween/projects/polymath-platform/packages/ui/src/components-native/LivingCard.web.tsx) files, no cross-platform leakage.

---

### 2d — URL-Based Deep Linking (Web Superpower)

**What:** Mobile deep links need app installed. Web gets this *free* — a URL is a shareable artifact.  
**How:** React Navigation already maps screen names to paths on web. We need to configure `linking` in `NavigationContainer`.

#### [MODIFY] [App.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Naween/projects/polymath-platform/apps/gurudevi-mobile/App.tsx)

```tsx
const linking = Platform.OS === 'web' ? {
  prefixes: ['https://app.gurudevi.edlove.org'],
  config: {
    screens: {
      Main: '',
      Auth: 'auth',
      AIAssistant: 'ai',
    }
  }
} : undefined;

<NavigationContainer linking={linking} ref={navigationRef}>
```

Teachers can now bookmark `app.gurudevi.edlove.org/ai` to jump directly to the AI assistant.

---

### 2e — Rich Clipboard Sharing (Web Only)

**What:** On mobile, "Share" opens native share sheet. On web, we can copy a rich-text link directly to clipboard (clipboard API supports HTML).  
**How:** `expo-clipboard` works on web. In community post share actions and profile linktree, add a web-specific "Copy Link" that generates a proper URL.

#### [MODIFY] community share handler — Pattern C

```ts
import * as Clipboard from 'expo-clipboard';

const sharePost = async (postId: string) => {
  if (Platform.OS === 'web') {
    await Clipboard.setStringAsync(`${window.location.origin}/community/${postId}`);
    showToast('Link copied to clipboard');
  } else {
    // existing native Share.share(...)
  }
};
```

---

### 2f — Better Auth URL Flow (Web-Specific)

**What:** Supabase OAuth on web lands on a callback URL with tokens in the fragment. Mobile uses deep links. Web browsers handle this differently.  
**How:** In Supabase project settings:
1. Set **Site URL** = `https://app.gurudevi.edlove.org`
2. Add it to **Redirect URLs** allowlist  
3. For Google OAuth — add origin to Google Cloud Console

> [!IMPORTANT]
> This is a **config change in Supabase dashboard**, not code. Without it, OAuth sign-in redirects to localhost or fails in production.

